ntdll: drop hangover's large-page warning — propnix supports that configuration.

Hangover prints this from setup_config_dir() on every launch whenever the host page size is not 4k:

    You are running with the wrong page size, expect problems!
    Please also consult https://github.com/AndreRH/hangover/wiki/Page-Size

For hangover that is fair warning: 4k is its supported configuration and anything else is the user's
problem. For propnix it is backwards. 16k IS the page size of the Apple Silicon hosts this tree targets,
it is the configuration the emulator stack is built and tested for, and the patches that make it work are
carried right here — the thread-stack guard headroom (0001), the host-page-aligned shared sections
(0007), and FEX's own 4k-guard-page assumption, patched in emulators/fex.

So the message reports our INTENDED configuration as a fault, on every single launch of every single
game, above whatever output actually matters. The cost is not the two lines; it is that a reader who sees
"expect problems!" before every game learns to skip wine's output, and then misses the diagnostic that is
genuinely about their problem. Anything page-size related that is still broken must say so at its own
call site, with its own range and numbers, the way 0007's fallback does.

Dropped rather than silenced behind a flag: a warning nobody is ever meant to see is dead code, and the
comment left in its place records why the configuration is deliberate for the next reader of this
function.
diff --git i/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c w/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
index 14b8bc77..a6f5e6e1 100644
--- i/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
+++ w/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
@@ -1325,10 +1325,12 @@ static int setup_config_dir(void)
     struct stat st;
     int fd_cwd = open( ".", O_RDONLY );
 
-#ifdef _SC_PAGESIZE
-    if (sysconf( _SC_PAGESIZE ) != 4096)
-        MESSAGE("You are running with the wrong page size, expect problems!\nPlease also consult https://github.com/AndreRH/hangover/wiki/Page-Size\n");
-#endif
+    /* Hangover warns here when the host page size is not 4k. propnix SUPPORTS that configuration
+     * deliberately — 16k is the page size of the Apple Silicon hosts this tree targets — and carries the
+     * patches that make it work (large-page stack guards, host-page-aligned shared sections, the FEX
+     * guard-page fix). A warning on every single launch of every game therefore reports our intended
+     * configuration as a fault, which trains the reader to ignore wine's output. Anything page-size
+     * related that is still genuinely broken must say so at its own call site instead. */
 
     if (chdir( config_dir ) == -1)
     {
